Well, just about everything went my way this game...I played an elf (Noid by
name) and got a wish on level 4.  I went for BlsRp+3 Mjolly.  Got everything
except the rustproofing, as I found to my dismay.  Only 1 shop, but 4 altars
(No priest(esse)s though.)  Got teleportation + control fairly soon.  Bones
level yields some good armor (+3 boots, +3 gloves, helm of telepathy -- HoT
pitched in hell thanks to rusting to -3) and ring of conflict.  Get +3 GDSM
from a throne-room wish.  Get Excalibur from dipping, but its -1.  Get to 
castle, 3 wishes total.  3 blessed scrolls of enchant weapon (Excalibur goes
from -1 to +8), +3 Shield of Reflection, 1 (drat!) blessed scroll of enchant 
armor.  Wand of polymorph yields lots of useless stuff, but do polymorph ~20
stones to 'white gems'.  Undoubtedly worthless glass, I play catch with every 
Unicorn I see to keep a high luck.  After getting the ring of levitation, I 
teleport to level 50 and slog my way up (getting 4(!) almulets of life saving
along the way! Only needed one...) killing all the major demons and Vladdy
before finding the wiz.  Bump him off, grab the amulet, and do teleports to
get up the stairs to level 1.  Collect from a treasure zoo and a few caches 
along the way (17K gold total).  Just as I get to the level 1 stairs,
the wizard puts in another appearance.  This time, he splits in two twice :(
and they begin attacking me like mad.  He calls for help which turns on him (I
loooove rings of conflict!  Ever seen a purple worm eat the wiz?) But even with
a ring of regeneration, 114 h.p. and -21 A.C. I go down.  One amulet of life
saving gone, 3 that I never need.  Finish the wizard off and ascend.  The end
game was, actually, uneventful.  Except for my blindfold getting cursed...but
the 1 potion of holy water that I have been saving for a rainy day rescues me.
Slap the amulet on the altar, and Poof!  Instant immortality. 2,065,014. Not
even close to my previous best of 60000.

